ory and with the advice of  miguel and ryan i managed to come up  with  some form of backstory number 11. you'd  be surprised how much was actually built  practically i feel that no one told them  that that isn't how films are made now  that you don't have to build the whole  castle king's landing was built  completely from the ground up and it was  twice as large as anyone could have  imagined it to be after reading the  scripts  you walk around these sets that look  like ancient monuments and buildings  with massive statues number 12 keep an  eye out for the visionary behind this  world george r.r martin may randomly pop  up in the series he did do a cameo in  the original game of thrones pilot but  unfortunately they ended up reshooting  most of the pilot so i was left on the  cutting room floor he was also supposed  to be a severed head but that idea got  nuked because they found out how  expensive a custom severed head would be  so they decided to go a cheaper route  they just bought a box of used severed  heads number 13. adaptations are tricky  ryan j condell found when it came to  bringing this book to the screen the  most difficult thing was the way it was  written george r.r martin calls the  novel a fake history book so when you're  reading it there is not a lot of  dialogue to go off of  you have point a and point c but you  don't really know what point b was  another complicated aspect of it was how  much time needs to be covered the story  goes on for generations i was figuring  out how to structure it in such a way  that we could move people through this  very complex timeline number fourteen  let's just say it was a big cast one  thing george rr martin loved about  making this show was that hbo didn't  limit him on how many characters were  allowed in the story in past reviews for  game of thrones critics would bash how  many characters the show had and how  hard it was to keep track of them um i  don't want to underestimate the  intelligence of the audience or the  readers you you can keep track of them  oftentimes when turning a novel into a  series they end up having to eliminate  or combine characters  george didn't want to do that the  audience is more sophisticated than  sometimes uh people making television  number 15. game of thrones has always  been all over the map  so it's safe to say house of the dragon  won't be any different for the interior  shots they camped up at leavesden  studios in england with several outdoor  shots in cornwall devon and surrey as  well as european locations like spain  and portugal with an incredible writer  director cast and crew behind george r.r  martin's legendary writing we couldn't  be more excited to devour everything  house of the dragon has to offer what  are you most excited to see
 

